!v024!^tEl gÇnero Megalomus Rambur (Neurop-planipennia-HemerobÅdae) en la Rep£blica Argentina y Chile
!v028!^aGonz†lez Olazo^bEnrique Vicente
!v045!1979
!v047!^eUniversidad Nacional de Tucum†n, Facultad de Ciencias Naturales^lTucum†n
!v048!AR
!v050!es
!v052!^e24 h.^iil., fot., mapa ; 30 cm.
!v055!^nSEMINARIO^sUNT-FCN^eUniversidad Nacional de Tucum†n, Facultad de Ciencias Naturales^gLicenciado^cLicenciatura en Ciencias Biol¢gicas - Orientaci¢n Zoolog°a^d1979
!v059!Ejemplar fotocopiado
!v059!Bibliograf°a al final
!v059!nß de orden interno: S-56
!v060!595.7
!v062!ZOOLOGIA
!v062!SEMINARIO
!v062!HEMEROBIIDAE
!v062!PLANIPENNIA
!v062!INSEPTOS
!v062!ENTOMOLOGIA
!v069!The present paper is the first of a series of revisions concerning Argentine and South American Hemerobiidae (Neuroptera-Planipennia). A general account of the family and a key for Argentine-Chilean genera are given. The generus Megalomus Rambur 1842 in Argentina and Chile is particularly treated, with the recognition of two subgenera: Megalomus and Pirionius. The genera Pirionius Nav†s 1926 and Spinomegalomus Nakahara 1965 are synonymized with Megalomus. The following new Synonymy is indicated: Megalomus linguatus Nav†s 1910 - Megalomus intricatus Navas 1914 = Megalomus infuscatus Nav†s 1914 = Megalomus princeps Nav†s 1932 = Megalomus nanus Nav†s 1933 = Megalomus bridaroll Nav†s 1933. A new species: Megalomus stangei is described. The paper is completed with schemes, photographs and maps.-
!v075!^c595.7^G589
